SUMMARY:Cedarock Park – Autumn Afternoon at the Homestead (Burlington)
DESCRIPTION:Come join NCWF Triad Wild! and Tri-County Conservationists Chapters with T. Gilbert Pearson Audubon Society for a leisurely nature outing at Alamance County’s Cedarock Park! Beginning at the Garrett Historical Farm\, participants will immerse themselves in late autumn homestead life with real farm animals on-site. \nWe will then meander down the Spoon Branch Trail to Rock Creek and back (with the option of completing the entire loop of this 1.3-mile trail)\, taking in as much wildlife as we can! Birders\, herpers\, and history lovers alike will enjoy this nature outing\, fit for nature and history enthusiasts of all ages. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/cedarock-park-autumn-afternoon-at-the-homestead-burlington/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/cedarock.jpg
END:VEVENT
